{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1129700-pyrokenesis-question","id":1129700,"title":"Pyrokenesis question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-15T23:43:58-07:00","id":1129700,"title":"Pyrokenesis question","content":"So, I was wondering.<br /> Say like my character wants to use pyrokenesis to control existing flames or electricity with her mind and attack someone with it.<br /> First I have to roll willpower for it yes but How fast is it? And for my opponent to dodge it he needs to have at least equal successes or exceed the number of successes of my arete roll or what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12133,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","user":"Leonardo","date":". 08-16-2017, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T06:55:11-07:00","id":1129766,"title":"","content":"It's fast as to take effect in one turn.<br /> <br /> An opponent needs to dodge whatever successes you used to make your &quot;attack roll&quot;. In revised this was Dextrety + Occult, if you used willpower to attack, it's willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T07:30:14-07:00","id":1129777,"title":"","content":"Idk it says willpower roll to control the flames. Isn't there an arete roll for it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T07:53:06-07:00","id":1129786,"title":"","content":"I can't know for certain in this case: I need to know what rule are you using, and from what book.<br /> <br /> I imagine that, if this is True Magick and not Sorcery, you first give yourself pyrokinetic skills through a normal Arete roll, and then (now that a fire has been made subject to your will) you use willpower to attack with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T07:55:29-07:00","id":1129787,"title":"","content":"It's in How do you do that page 36.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T08:32:44-07:00","id":1129801,"title":"","content":"I found for myself the -kinesis rules in hdydt very out of place.<br /> It's one of those examples that mixes focus with rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T11:35:59-07:00","id":1129905,"title":"","content":"What's wrong with a plain and simple Arete roll for a Forces 2 effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T16:51:01-07:00","id":1130047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leonardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1129700-pyrokenesis-question?p=1129787#post1129787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's in How do you do that page 36.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's your problem. You're taking HDYDT seriously.<br /> <br /> That book has problems, in that it adds complexity where it isn't needed, usually for the sole reason of adhering to a particular interpretation of Focus. Except Magick itself isn't meant to work differently based on the Paradigm. It's all meant to function the same, for ease of play. Like lastlostboy said, it blends Focus with mechanics in a way the game was never designed to. Another example of this is how Akashic Effects as described in HDYDT all require the addition of Prime and Quintessence expenditure, when the same Effects performed by any other type of mage wouldn't. All because &quot;Chi&quot; as a metaphysical concept used to justify a mage's powers is conflated to Quintessence in a blunt fashion.<br /> <br /> What, exactly, is the mechanical difference between a mage using &quot;psychic powers&quot; to summon and direct fire, versus a wizard using a magic wand to do the same thing? In every other book released for Mage: The Ascension, not a damn thing. HDYDT is the single outlier, and it makes the game unfair if its directions are followed blindly. Unfair for players, because one player might be saddled with extra restrictions and hoops to jump through, while another player is not.<br /> <br /> Like I say to anyone reading HDYDT, that everything the book says with a grain of salt. We on the board here like to call it Phil Brucato's Book of House Rules for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T00:36:08-07:00","id":1130168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1129700-pyrokenesis-question?p=1130047#post1130047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there's your problem. You're taking HDYDT seriously.<br /> <br /> Like I say to anyone reading HDYDT, that everything the book says with a grain of salt. We on the board here like to call it Phil Brucato's Book of House Rules for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in agreement. With HDYDT, you need to cheerry-pick things you like and other things you simply ignore.<br /> <br /> That said, I've already stated in another threat that I see *one* good logical reason of allowing a flavor of 'psionic' pyromancers in the way that HDYDT describes - and that is that the chracter substitutes usage of complex tools with mere concentration, hence the Willpower roll.<br /> They do not need to chant, gesture, dance, or perform anything aside of simply concentrate. The Willpower roll *is* their roll for using their tool, same as a dancer would roll athletics or the like. And it's quite a powerful tool in its simplicity early on.<br /> <br /> It's not quite the same Bad Idea as HDYDT's treatment of Chi always needing Prime-and-Quint, and Shamans needing to mix Spirit into all their effects.<br /> The Pyromancer Willpower angle has actual merit if you treat it from the tool point of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T02:02:48-07:00","id":1130176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1129700-pyrokenesis-question?p=1130168#post1130168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not quite the same Bad Idea as HDYDT's treatment of Chi always needing Prime-and-Quint, and Shamans needing to mix Spirit into all their effects.<br /> The Pyromancer Willpower angle has actual merit if you treat it from the tool point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>I concur, only use as much of HDYDT as one needs.<br /> <br /> This &quot;mixing&quot; is also in the Mind Sphere description pp 519-520 of M20: &quot;Combined with Correspondence, Forces, Matter, or Life, he is able to employ telekinesis, pyrokinetics, and psychophysical assault, influencing objects, elements, or people with the power of his mind.&quot; HDYDT gives the helpful description of Mind 3/Forces 2 (Difficulty 6/7/8)...a bit of a tax for the mentalist considering the same thing should be able to be done with just Forces 2 (Difficulty 5/6/7). What HDYDT is telling us is that the more in tune with your paradigm/practices you are, the harder it is for you to do magic! <br /> <br /> Actually, is there any real penalty to combined sphere effects, if the spheres are the same rank? Is there any fundamental difference between Corr2/Forces 2 and Forces 2? I had always played as not, that differences come into play when you include higher level spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13778-cerulean-scream","name":"Cerulean Scream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13778_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T02:33:07-07:00","id":1130182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1129700-pyrokenesis-question?p=1130047#post1130047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another example of this is how Akashic Effects as described in HDYDT all require the addition of Prime and Quintessence expenditure, when the same Effects performed by any other type of mage wouldn't. All because &quot;Chi&quot; as a metaphysical concept used to justify a mage's powers is conflated to Quintessence in a blunt fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>EXACTLY!</b><br /> <br /> And I hate it - the book - for it. Because it's a noob mistake!<br /> It was a book designed to help rookies to understand how they build their own effects with their spheres. To show them what is possible.<br /> And it ended up as a... spell book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1129700-pyrokenesis-question?p=1130047#post1130047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, exactly, is the mechanical difference between a mage using &quot;psychic powers&quot; to summon and direct fire, versus a wizard using a magic wand to do the same thing? In every other book released for Mage: The Ascension, not a damn thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you follow the -kinesis-concept of creating a dynamic magic effect that allows you to use static magic it ends where you weave a spell, that allows you a change reality without paradox because &quot;it's just the effect of the spell&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sorry but that misses totally the point of Mage. :/<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1129700-pyrokenesis-question?p=1130168#post1130168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and that is that the chracter substitutes usage of complex tools with mere concentration, hence the Willpower roll.<br /> They do not need to chant, gesture, dance, or perform anything aside of simply concentrate. The Willpower roll *is* their roll for using their tool, same as a dancer would roll athletics or the like. And it's quite a powerful tool in its simplicity early on.</div> </div> </div> </div>The willpower roll is not the problem. The implication that the effect has a pre-designed tool - in this case Thought Forms - is. In which case the willpower roll would be indeed the &quot;use&quot; of the tool.<br /> But every effect in the book should be independent of the tools a mage uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12609,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","user":"lastlostboy","date":". 08-17-2017, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T05:00:33-07:00","id":1130209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lastlostboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1129700-pyrokenesis-question?p=1130182#post1130182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The willpower roll is not the problem. It's the implication that the effect has a pre-designed tool - in this case Thought Forms - is. In which case the willpower roll would be indeed the &quot;use&quot; of the tool.<br /> But every effect in the book should be independent of the tools a mage uses.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. it should have been under a heading of 'Using concentration/psionics as a tool'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T05:01:45-07:00","id":1130210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cerulean Scream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1129700-pyrokenesis-question?p=1130176#post1130176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, is there any real penalty to combined sphere effects, if the spheres are the same rank? Is there any fundamental difference between Corr2/Forces 2 and Forces 2? I had always played as not, that differences come into play when you include higher level spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Newp, no penalties. The difficulty is always based on the single highest sphere used, so it makes no idfference if you use one, two, or all nine level 2 spheres for something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T17:43:06-07:00","id":1130618,"title":"","content":"I agree with all the critics to HDYDT. That being said:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Willpower roll *is* their roll for using their tool, same as a dancer would roll athletics or the like. And it's quite a powerful tool in its simplicity early on.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12133\" data-vbnamecard=\"12133\">Leonardo</a> : The Willpower roll it's your Focus, and your Instrument. It shouldn't be described a mandatory part of your Focus (complex combination of Paradigm, Practice and Instrument), but well, that has been covered...<br /> <br /> You use Arete to do a clasic Forces 2+ effect, that in HDYDT uses an addition of Mind 3 as &quot;Sphere Tax&quot; (the book punishes you for wanting to use psychic phenomena as a focus, which it's a very distasteful way to do things). You roll Arete as normal to calculate the damage/how much fire you move.<br /> <br /> In M20 if you use a gun as a tool, the enemy needs to dodge the successes you got in Firearms + Dextrety much like dodging a normal shot. Thus, if you use Willpower as a focus, your enemy has to evade the successes you got on the Willpower roll. That's how things are. <hr /><br /> I think this &quot;dodge magick&quot; rules are far from perfect, but you can reduce or increase the difficulty depending on how easy or hard to evade you think that a certain spell should be (as with any roll).<br /> <br /> As a house rule, I wouldn't allow to evade Arete successes <i>directly </i>in the case of mystical focuses (like a magick wand), that makes wands easier to evade than plasma guns or punches, instead I would tell the mystic to do an Occult/Esoterica + Wits roll if the spell needs to be &quot;targeted&quot; (if it doesn't need to be targeted, then it can't be evaded), like in Revised Edition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-17-2017, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T04:02:12-07:00","id":1131178,"title":"","content":"Just a thought. In order to make all this psychic stuff actually a benefit, why not make it so the Mind 3 sphere tax actually allows you to use WP to augment the spell or something.<br /> <br /> For example. Perhaps the Arete roll is is for the Mind 3 effect, after which point you'll be able to roll WP to do the Forces 2 effect. This way, you get a tangible benefit since we have a tangible benefit as you will always be rolling more dice with WP than with Arete alone. It could even be that each bonus success on the Arete roll could translate to more dice to roll along side your WP.<br /> <br /> This also gives Psychic type mages an incentive to invest more into WP than into Arete, which is always a good thing.<br /> <br /> What stops this from being easily exploited? You will still need the ranks in the spheres of all the other effects. Corr or Forces or whatever for Telekenisis, Forces for Pyrokenisis, etc.<br /> Also, you would need to have Mind at the level above the highest level of the other spheres involved. So moving fire about with Mind 3 is fine, but if you wanted to turn fire into electricity with the power of your mind, you'd need Forces 3 and Mind 4 to get that lovely WP boost.<br /> <br /> Another important distinction would be that, unlike Arete rolls, you would not be able to &quot;build&quot; the effect. Once you've rolled your WP plus extra dice, that's it, that's your effect.<br /> <br /> One way to think of it is, Pure Forces effects would just be an Arete roll you can build for direct damage. Psychic effects would be an Arete roll which acts like an Attack roll you can build, and a WP roll which acts like a damage roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T11:47:40-07:00","id":1132321,"title":"","content":"I tend to disagree with most of you. I like HDYDT a lot. I usually discard some things, but I use most of it. Concerning pyrokenesis, I make the difference between the blatant Forces 3 Effect that would allow the Mage to project flames or make fireballs, etc and the Pyrokenesis Mind 3 / Forces 3 Effect. This one allow the Mage to use fire as he/she wills it, giving it form and transforming it to an extension of the Mage. I play it that way : split the successes between damage (how much fire do you control with your mind, at which intensity ?) and duration (how many rounds will you control it ?) as usual. Then, the Willpower rolls are there to use in replacement of attack rolls since Dexterity+Firearms do not really apply... If you find another skill to roll the attack, that's fine I guess. Willpower is as good as any.<br /> <br /> I tend to use HDYDT as a guidline and like many times, in the end, the ST is the last judge of what is to use or not, don't you think ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T12:31:34-07:00","id":1132357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1129700-pyrokenesis-question?p=1132321#post1132321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to use HDYDT as a guidline and like many times, in the end, the ST is the last judge of what is to use or not, don't you think ?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a ST idea guideline, it's not too bad. It's how it advertises itself as a tutorial of the sphere system for new players that most people have a problem with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}